A||||10||RossT||Tom or anyone, what do you think of Wisconsin Fiero Dells run??||||1||
Z||000000||RossT||01-28-2000||03:43 AM||||I am thinking of attending this years Wisconsin Fiero Dells Run car show. It would be my first fiero show, and was wondering what you guys think. Its about a 750 mile drive for me. Is it worth attending?||||reg||1
Z||000001||JetroGT||01-28-2000||04:59 AM||||Every year it gets better. This year it's a four day event. A couple years ago I won gray fiero store floor mats in the raffle. Most of the fiero venders are there, Bob Stiger, Rodney Dickman, and some others that I can't rember. If you are able to go, go. And bring lots of film. If you can't get a room at Chula Vista, their are lot's of other places to stay in the Dells. Most of which are booked on the weekends. One of the new resorts is the Black Wolf Lodge. Very nice. It has what looks to be indoor water slides. Last year someone from New York attended the show. The whole way to the show he must have used up 40 or more fuel pump fuses. Before he left he had the pump replaced in his white 88 GT. I guess one of the motor wires was shorting out on the frame, blowing the fuse. If you look on the fiero fanitics of Wisconsin you will find lots of photos of the carshow on various years. I hope this helps you.||||reg||6
Z||000002||TOM||01-28-2000||11:07 AM||||Living in sunny so cal I have no idea||||reg||1
Z||000003||WKDFIRO||01-28-2000||12:42 PM||||According to one of my colleagues, John Parentii it is a very well organized immensely fun time not to be missed. Worth 750 miles of a trip? Thats pushing the limits I would want to be in a Fiero but thats just me.||||reg||14
Z||000004||RossT||01-28-2000||01:55 PM||||I meant Dave not Tom, sorry. Thanks guys, I think that I will give it a go.  Ross||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phil||01-28-2000||02:24 PM||||Does anyone else have troubles taking long trips in a Fiero? I've taken 2 round trips from RI to FL (one with the wife and one solo)and experienced no discomfort what so ever and that's doing 600+mi a day.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Dave85||01-28-2000||03:36 PM||||I took a round trip to Colorado Springs CO from Fayetteville AR. I was having so much fun driving that I never stopped. I spent 40 hrs. behind the wheel.  I was a little tired but not uncomfortable.  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Greg Piet||01-28-2000||05:01 PM||||When is it?<BR>I am going to WI in the summertime, and if possible I could modify my schedule to show up as well.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||DRH||01-28-2000||05:10 PM||||June 1-4, see this link:<P> <A HREF="http://argo.acronet.net/~abarthel/dells.html" TARGET=_blank>http://argo.acronet.net/~abarthel/dells.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||DRH||01-28-2000||05:16 PM||||My daughter was in state playoffs for high school soccer last year so I didn't make it. I know... I know... she wasn't playing the WHOLE weekend... Bad Fiero Owner!!!<P>Anyway, on the way to one of her games that Thursday we passed 20 or 30 Fieros lined up to go into a resteraunt in a town a few miles down the road. Awesome site!!!<P>I'm going to try to make it between games  this year.<P>David.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Standard||01-28-2000||05:23 PM||||I really hope to make it to the Dell run, it looks like a ton of fun.. it would be my first Fiero show, also.  I have no problems making long trips in any kind of car.. I just drove to Winona this morning, 2.5 hour drive for me.. not terribly long but it's a fun drive.||||reg||14
